      },
      "lineNbr": 97,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-06T09:39:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do we really need to keep both the object and its serialized CBOR representation at the same time? Additionally, I noticed that the CborSerializable [1] trait in  coset also consumes the object when converting it to a vector.\n\n[1] https://docs.rs/coset/0.3.4/coset/trait.CborSerializable.html",
      "parentUuid": "c66a2061_fab1ce37",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 97,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 97,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "99916fdbd240341e9adabafffc8535c36259603a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
